    {
      "id": "arrival",
      "kind": "chapter",
      "title": "Arrival",
      "number": 1,
      "opener": true,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "_b1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The ferry came in sideways, as it always did, shouldering the tide. From the rail the town looked like a sentence somebody had started with confidence and then abandoned: a bright row of houses, a comma of breakwater, and after that only weather."
            }
          ],
          "style": "dropcap"
        },
        {
          "id": "_b2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Nobody met the boat. The gulls conducted their usual inquiry. A man in an oilskin was coiling rope with the patience of someone who intends to coil it again tomorrow, and the harbour clock, which had been wrong for so long that people navigated by its error, said a quarter past something."
            }
          ],
          "style": "body"
        },
        {
          "id": "_b3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "She had come for the archive, or that was what the letter said. The letter also said "
            },
            {
              "text": "bring boots",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", which she had taken for a joke until she saw the quay. It was the kind of quay that keeps what it is given."
            }
          ],
          "style": "body"
        },
        {
          "id": "_b4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The first thing anyone tells you here is the time of the next low water."
            }
          ],
          "style": "lead"
        },
        {
          "id": "_b13",
          "type": "group",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "quay",
              "type": "heading",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The quay"
                }
              ],
              "level": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "_b6",
              "type": "image",
              "resource": "pic",
              "caption": [
                {
                  "text": "Fig. 1. The harbour at dusk, "
                },
                {
                  "text": "looking west",
                  "italic": true
                },
                {
                  "text": "."
                }
              ],
              "width": 0.7,
              "fit": "contain"
            },
            {
              "id": "_b7",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "There is a particular light on a coast in the last hour, when the water gives back more than the sky sends down. Painters have a word for it and so do pilots, and the two words do not agree. The painters mean that the edges of things go soft; the pilots mean that you can no longer trust a distance."
                }
              ],
              "style": "body"
            },
            {
              "id": "_b8",
              "type": "gallery",
              "resources": [
                "pic",
                "map"
              ],
              "caption": [
                {
                  "text": "Two views of the same water."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "_b10",
              "type": "box",
              "style": "bar",
              "title": "Note",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "_b9",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "Mind the "
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "gap",
                      "bold": true
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " between the pontoon and the steps."
                    }
                  ],
                  "style": "small"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "_b12",
              "type": "box",
              "style": "bar",
              "title": "Warning",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "_b11",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "Spring tides run two hours late here."
                    }
                  ],
                  "style": "small"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "_b23",
          "type": "group",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "_b14",
              "type": "heading",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "What the tide left"
                }
              ],
              "level": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "_b15",
              "type": "quote",
              "paragraphs": [
                [
                  {
                    "text": "A coast is a sentence the sea keeps rewriting."
                  }
                ]
              ],
              "attribution": [
                {
                  "text": "Harbour proverb"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "_b16",
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": true,
              "items": [
                [
                  {
                    "text": "Rope, tarred, about four fathoms."
                  }
                ],
                [
                  {
                    "text": "A "
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "brass",
                    "bold": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " sounding lead with the tallow still in it."
                  }
                ],
                [
                  {
                    "text": "One boot. Nobody asks about the other."
                  }
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "_b17",
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                [
                  {
                    "text": "Limpets"
                  }
                ],
                [
                  {
                    "text": "Bladderwrack"
                  }
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "_b18",
              "type": "divider",
              "style": "rule"
            },
            {
              "id": "_b19",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The tide kept its accounts in the old way,",
                  "break": true
                },
                {
                  "text": "a line of wrack for every hour it stayed,",
                  "break": true
                },
                {
                  "text": "and what it took it entered as a loan."
                }
              ],
              "style": "verse",
              "align": "center"
            },
            {
              "id": "_b20",
              "type": "divider",
              "style": "ornament"
            },
            {
              "id": "_b21",
              "type": "video",
              "resource": "clip",
              "caption": [
                {
                  "text": "A study in two colours."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "_b22",
              "type": "audio",
              "resource": "sound",
              "caption": [
                {
                  "text": "The same study, for the ear."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "_b24",
          "type": "heading",
          "spans": [
